/*
==============================================================================
  OID4VCI  A1  —  IAE Cross-Session Holder-Binding Confusion
  Interactive Authorization Endpoint (Presentation-During-Issuance)
==============================================================================

  Tool:           Tamarin Prover 1.12.0 / Maude 3.5.1 (verified on this version)
  Spec analysed:  OpenID for Verifiable Credential Issuance, Interactive
                  Authorization Endpoint (IAE), v1.1 editor's draft.
                  Sections: §6 (IAE), §6.2.1.4 (Preventing Session Fixation),
                  Appendix A.2.5 / A.3.5 (Holder-Binding "iar:" audience).
  Companion:      Security & Trust in the OpenID4VC Ecosystem (Fett /
                  Lodderstedt), §4.3 holder-binding requirements I-40, P-50.


==============================================================================
  FOUR CONFIGURATIONS — pass exactly one -D flag at runtime
==============================================================================

  -DVULNERABLE   Spec-as-written. The Issuer (acting as OpenID4VP Verifier)
                 binds the required presentation to (a) the opaque server-side
                 auth_session handle, (b) the "iar:<IAE-URL>" audience, and (c)
                 the OpenID4VP nonce associated with auth_session per §6.2.1.4.
                 It does NOT bind the holder key of the presented VP to the
                 holder key the freshly issued credential is bound to.

  -DFIXED_NONCE  NEGATIVE RESULT. Binds the presentation nonce into the
                 issuance key-proof and checks it equals the auth_session
                 nonce. Does NOT close A1: the nonce is public (it ships in the
                 require-interaction response), so any party freshly mints a
                 proof over ITS OWN key carrying that nonce.

  -DFIXED        PRIMARY FIX (holder-key continuity). Issuer requires the
                 issuance key-proof to verify under, and the issued credential
                 to be bound to, the holder key that produced the accepted VP.

  -DFIXED_TXDATA STRONGER / MORE FLEXIBLE FIX. The presenting holder commits,
                 inside its KB-JWT, to h(pkH_iss) of the (possibly fresh) key
                 the new credential should be bound to. Issuer checks
                 h(key-proof.pkH) = commitment. Closes A1 while permitting
                 per-credential key separation (pkH_iss != pkH_pres) for
                 unlinkability.


==============================================================================
  THE ATTACK A1 (cross-session holder-binding confusion)
==============================================================================

  CI offers "presentation during issuance": to obtain a derived credential the
  wallet must present an existing credential. CI acts as an OpenID4VP Verifier;
  the new credential's subject is taken from the PRESENTED credential, while its
  holder-binding key is taken from the ISSUANCE key-proof. §6 mandates NO
  cryptographic linkage between these two holder keys.

  Adversary: a malicious / compromised split-architecture wallet backend
  (§13.4) -- equivalently a Dolev-Yao attacker driving its own auth_session and
  relaying the honest holder's presentation. Issuer honest; prerequisite issuer
  PI honest; victim honest with un-leaked holder key.

  Trace: attacker opens auth_session_A -> CI returns signed presReq (nonce_A,
  aud iar:CI) -> attacker relays it to the victim -> victim returns a VP bound
  to (iar:CI, nonce_A) under skH_pres -> attacker submits (auth_session_A, VP)
  -> CI accepts (nonce_A == auth_session_A nonce, §6.2.1.4 SATISFIED) and mints
  an AT bound to auth_session_A storing pkH_pres + the victim's subject ->
  attacker sends a Credential Request with a key-proof under ITS OWN key ->
  CI, finding no requirement that the proof key equal pkH_pres, issues a
  credential carrying the VICTIM's subject bound to the ATTACKER's key.

  Why §6.2.1.4 does not help: it only forces nonce == auth_session; nonce_A
  does match. The missing link is pkH_pres = pkH_proof.
  Why stock abstractions do not rule it out: TLS-as-confidential-channel and
  EUF-CMA both hold; k_pres and k_proof are different terms with no relating
  equation. It is a binding failure, not an interception.


==============================================================================
  ABSTRACTIONS
==============================================================================

  A1. TLS -> Dolev-Yao In/Out.
  A2. OAuth/PAR + Token Endpoint folded into one opaque, session-bound Access
      Token aToken/3 (private) minted by the IAE verify step and gating the
      Credential Endpoint (issue #225: the access token still gates the request).
  A3. DPoP OMITTED: it sender-constrains the AT to the client's transport key,
      not the holder/issuance key, so it gives no uplift against A1.
  A4. Carry-and-verify for the presented VC (plain signing has no message
      recovery): subject and holder key travel in the VP and the Issuer
      reconstructs the signed payload and checks it with verify().
  A5. Single derived-credential dataset.
  A6. PI honest, issues only to honest holders (the attacker cannot mint itself
      a prerequisite VC). A1 hijacks the honest holder's presentation; it does
      not require the attacker to present.
  A7. "Cross-session": the attacker opens its own auth_session and consumes a
      presentation the victim produced for the (relayed, Issuer-signed) request.


==============================================================================
  HOW TO RUN
==============================================================================

  tamarin-prover --prove -DVULNERABLE    --auto-sources OID4VCI_A1_IAE_holder_binding_v2.spthy
  tamarin-prover --prove -DFIXED_NONCE   --auto-sources OID4VCI_A1_IAE_holder_binding_v2.spthy
  tamarin-prover --prove -DFIXED         --auto-sources OID4VCI_A1_IAE_holder_binding_v2.spthy
  tamarin-prover --prove -DFIXED_TXDATA  --auto-sources OID4VCI_A1_IAE_holder_binding_v2.spthy

==============================================================================
*/

theory OID4VCI_A1 begin

builtins: signing, hashing

functions:  penc/3, pdec/2
equations:  pdec(penc(m, pk(k), r), k) = m

functions:  aToken/3 [private]


// ============================================================================
//                                MACROS
// ============================================================================

macros:

  iarAud(CI) = <'iar', CI>,

  presReqPayload(CI, nonce)        = <'openid4vp-request', CI, iarAud(CI), nonce>,
  presReqSigned(CI, nonce, ltkCI)  = <presReqPayload(CI, nonce),
                                      sign(presReqPayload(CI, nonce), ltkCI)>,

  prereqPayload(PI, sub, pkH)      = <'prereq-vc', PI, sub, pkH>,
  prereqVC(PI, sub, pkH, ltkPI)    = sign(prereqPayload(PI, sub, pkH), ltkPI),

  kbPayload(CI, nonce)             = <'kb-jwt', iarAud(CI), nonce>,
  kbProof(CI, nonce, skH)          = sign(kbPayload(CI, nonce), skH),

  kbPayloadTx(CI, nonce, cmt)      = <'kb-jwt-tx', iarAud(CI), nonce, cmt>,
  kbProofTx(CI, nonce, cmt, skH)   = sign(kbPayloadTx(CI, nonce, cmt), skH),

  keyProofPayload(CI, pkH)         = <'oid4vci-proof', CI, pkH>,
  keyProofJWT(CI, pkH, skH)        = sign(keyProofPayload(CI, pkH), skH),

  keyProofPayloadN(CI, pkH, nonce) = <'oid4vci-proof-n', CI, pkH, nonce>,
  keyProofJWTN(CI, pkH, nonce, skH)= sign(keyProofPayloadN(CI, pkH, nonce), skH),

  credPayload(CI, sub, pkH)        = <'credential', CI, sub, pkH>,
  credentialSig(CI, sub, pkH, ltkCI) = sign(credPayload(CI, sub, pkH), ltkCI)


// ============================================================================
//                              PREDICATES
// ============================================================================

predicates:
  HonestCI(CI)              <=> not (Ex #r. Reveal_CI(CI) @ r),
  NoHolderKeyLeak(Wid, pkH) <=> not (Ex #r. Reveal_HolderKey(Wid, pkH) @ r)


// ============================================================================
//                              RESTRICTIONS
// ============================================================================

restriction Eq:
  "All x y #i. Eq(x,y) @ i ==> x = y"

restriction OnlyOnceV:
  "All x #i #j. OnlyOnceV(x) @ i & OnlyOnceV(x) @ j ==> #i = #j"


// ============================================================================
//                          PARTY SETUP  (config-independent)
// ============================================================================

rule Register_CI [color=#fef3c7, role="Setup"]:
    [ Fr(~ltkCI) ]
  --[ Register_CI($CI), CIKey($CI, ~ltkCI), OnlyOnceV(<'reg-ci', $CI>) ]->
    [ !Ltk_CI($CI, ~ltkCI), !Pk_CI($CI, pk(~ltkCI)), Out(pk(~ltkCI)) ]

rule Register_PI [color=#fef3c7, role="Setup"]:
    [ Fr(~ltkPI) ]
  --[ Register_PI($PI), OnlyOnceV(<'reg-pi', $PI>) ]->
    [ !Ltk_PI($PI, ~ltkPI), !Pk_PI($PI, pk(~ltkPI)), Out(pk(~ltkPI)) ]

rule Issue_Prerequisite_VC [color=#fef3c7, role="Setup"]:
  let
    pkH = pk(~skH)
    vc  = prereqVC($PI, $sub, pkH, ~ltkPI)
  in
    [ Fr(~skH), !Ltk_PI($PI, ~ltkPI) ]
  --[ VictimKeyFresh($Wid, ~skH, pkH),
      PrereqIssued($PI, $Wid, $sub, pkH) ]->
    [ !Victim_PrereqVC($Wid, $PI, $sub, ~skH, pkH, vc),
      !StoredVictimHolderKey($Wid, ~skH, pkH) ]

rule Adversary_Wallet_Key [color=#fecaca, role="Adv"]:
    [ Fr(~skAdv) ] --[ AdversaryKey(pk(~skAdv)) ]-> [ Out(~skAdv) ]


// ============================================================================
//                            REVEAL RULES
// ============================================================================

rule Reveal_CI_Ltk [color=#fecaca, role="Adv"]:
    [ !Ltk_CI($CI, ~ltkCI) ] --[ Reveal_CI($CI) ]-> [ Out(~ltkCI) ]

rule Reveal_VictimHolderKey [color=#fecaca, role="Adv"]:
    [ !StoredVictimHolderKey($Wid, ~skH, pkH) ]
  --[ Reveal_HolderKey($Wid, pkH) ]->
    [ Out(~skH) ]


// ============================================================================
//   ISSUER IAE — STEP 1: require a presentation   (config-independent)
// ============================================================================

rule CI_IAE_Require_Presentation [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    presReq = presReqSigned($CI, ~nonce, ~ltkCI)
  in
    [ In(<'iae-init', $CI>),
      !Ltk_CI($CI, ~ltkCI),
      Fr(~authSess), Fr(~nonce) ]
  --[ CI_IAE_Start($CI, ~authSess, ~nonce) ]->
    [ !CI_IAE_Pending($CI, ~authSess, ~nonce),
      Out(<'iae-require-interaction', ~authSess, presReq>) ]


// ============================================================================
//   ISSUER IAE — STEP 2: verify presentation, mint Access Token
//   (§6.2.1.4: the KB-JWT nonce is checked against the auth_session nonce)
// ============================================================================

#ifdef VULNERABLE
rule CI_IAE_Verify_Presentation [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    vp = <'vp', $PI, sub, pkH_pres, vc, kbp>
    AT = aToken(~atSecret, authSess, $CI)
  in
    [ In(<'iae-followup', $CI, authSess, vp>),
      !CI_IAE_Pending($CI, authSess, nonce),
      !Pk_PI($PI, pkPI),
      Fr(~atSecret) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(vc,  prereqPayload($PI, sub, pkH_pres), pkPI)    = true ),
      _restrict( verify(kbp, kbPayload($CI, nonce),             pkH_pres) = true ),
      CI_Accepted_Presentation($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      OnlyOnceV(<'presented', authSess>) ]->
    [ !CI_Authorized($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      Out(AT) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED_NONCE
rule CI_IAE_Verify_Presentation [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    vp = <'vp', $PI, sub, pkH_pres, vc, kbp>
    AT = aToken(~atSecret, authSess, $CI)
  in
    [ In(<'iae-followup', $CI, authSess, vp>),
      !CI_IAE_Pending($CI, authSess, nonce),
      !Pk_PI($PI, pkPI),
      Fr(~atSecret) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(vc,  prereqPayload($PI, sub, pkH_pres), pkPI)    = true ),
      _restrict( verify(kbp, kbPayload($CI, nonce),             pkH_pres) = true ),
      CI_Accepted_Presentation($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      OnlyOnceV(<'presented', authSess>) ]->
    [ !CI_Authorized($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      Out(AT) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED
rule CI_IAE_Verify_Presentation [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    vp = <'vp', $PI, sub, pkH_pres, vc, kbp>
    AT = aToken(~atSecret, authSess, $CI)
  in
    [ In(<'iae-followup', $CI, authSess, vp>),
      !CI_IAE_Pending($CI, authSess, nonce),
      !Pk_PI($PI, pkPI),
      Fr(~atSecret) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(vc,  prereqPayload($PI, sub, pkH_pres), pkPI)    = true ),
      _restrict( verify(kbp, kbPayload($CI, nonce),             pkH_pres) = true ),
      CI_Accepted_Presentation($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      OnlyOnceV(<'presented', authSess>) ]->
    [ !CI_Authorized($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      Out(AT) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED_TXDATA
rule CI_IAE_Verify_Presentation [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    vp = <'vp-tx', $PI, sub, pkH_pres, cmt, vc, kbp>
    AT = aToken(~atSecret, authSess, $CI)
  in
    [ In(<'iae-followup', $CI, authSess, vp>),
      !CI_IAE_Pending($CI, authSess, nonce),
      !Pk_PI($PI, pkPI),
      Fr(~atSecret) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(vc,  prereqPayload($PI, sub, pkH_pres), pkPI)    = true ),
      _restrict( verify(kbp, kbPayloadTx($CI, nonce, cmt),      pkH_pres) = true ),
      CI_Accepted_Presentation($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      CI_Accepted_Commitment($CI, authSess, cmt),
      OnlyOnceV(<'presented', authSess>) ]->
    [ !CI_Authorized_Tx($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce, cmt),
      Out(AT) ]
#endif


// ============================================================================
//   HONEST HOLDER — PRESENTATION  (standalone; relay-able by the network)
// ============================================================================

#ifdef VULNERABLE
rule Victim_Present_VP [color=#d1fae5, role="Holder"]:
  let
    reqPayload = presReqPayload(CI, nonce)
    kbp        = kbProof(CI, nonce, ~skH)
    vp         = <'vp', $PI, sub, pkH, vc, kbp>
  in
    [ !Victim_PrereqVC($Wid, $PI, sub, ~skH, pkH, vc),
      !Pk_CI(CI, pkCI),
      In(<reqPayload, sig>) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(sig, reqPayload, pkCI) = true ),
      Victim_Presented($Wid, CI, pkH, sub, nonce) ]->
    [ Out(vp) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED_NONCE
rule Victim_Present_VP [color=#d1fae5, role="Holder"]:
  let
    reqPayload = presReqPayload(CI, nonce)
    kbp        = kbProof(CI, nonce, ~skH)
    vp         = <'vp', $PI, sub, pkH, vc, kbp>
  in
    [ !Victim_PrereqVC($Wid, $PI, sub, ~skH, pkH, vc),
      !Pk_CI(CI, pkCI),
      In(<reqPayload, sig>) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(sig, reqPayload, pkCI) = true ),
      Victim_Presented($Wid, CI, pkH, sub, nonce) ]->
    [ Out(vp) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED
rule Victim_Present_VP [color=#d1fae5, role="Holder"]:
  let
    reqPayload = presReqPayload(CI, nonce)
    kbp        = kbProof(CI, nonce, ~skH)
    vp         = <'vp', $PI, sub, pkH, vc, kbp>
  in
    [ !Victim_PrereqVC($Wid, $PI, sub, ~skH, pkH, vc),
      !Pk_CI(CI, pkCI),
      In(<reqPayload, sig>) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(sig, reqPayload, pkCI) = true ),
      Victim_Presented($Wid, CI, pkH, sub, nonce) ]->
    [ Out(vp) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED_TXDATA
rule Victim_Present_VP [color=#d1fae5, role="Holder"]:
  let
    reqPayload = presReqPayload(CI, nonce)
    pkHiss     = pk(~skHiss)
    cmt        = h(pkHiss)
    kbp        = kbProofTx(CI, nonce, cmt, ~skH)
    vp         = <'vp-tx', $PI, sub, pkH, cmt, vc, kbp>
  in
    [ !Victim_PrereqVC($Wid, $PI, sub, ~skH, pkH, vc),
      !Pk_CI(CI, pkCI),
      Fr(~skHiss),
      In(<reqPayload, sig>) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(sig, reqPayload, pkCI) = true ),
      Victim_Presented($Wid, CI, pkH, sub, nonce),
      Victim_Committed($Wid, pkHiss),
      IssuanceKeyFresh($Wid, ~skHiss, pkHiss) ]->
    [ Out(vp),
      !StoredIssuanceKey($Wid, ~skHiss, pkHiss) ]
#endif


// ============================================================================
//   HONEST ISSUANCE CLIENT  (drives the benign flow -> executability)
// ============================================================================

rule Hon_Client_Init [color=#bfdbfe, role="Wallet"]:
    [ !StoredVictimHolderKey($Wid, ~skH, pkH), Fr(~sid) ]
  --[ Hon_Init($Wid, $CI, ~sid) ]->
    [ Hon_St1($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skH, pkH), Out(<'iae-init', $CI>) ]

rule Hon_Client_Followup [color=#bfdbfe, role="Wallet"]:
  let
    reqPayload = presReqPayload($CI, nonce)
  in
    [ Hon_St1($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skH, pkH),
      !Pk_CI($CI, pkCI),
      In(<'iae-require-interaction', authSess, <reqPayload, sig>>),
      In(vp) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(sig, reqPayload, pkCI) = true ),
      Hon_Followup($Wid, $CI, ~sid, authSess, nonce) ]->
    [ Hon_St2($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skH, pkH, authSess, nonce),
      Out(<'iae-followup', $CI, authSess, vp>) ]

#ifdef VULNERABLE
rule Hon_Client_CredReq [color=#bfdbfe, role="Wallet"]:
  let
    pkE      = pk(~skE)
    keyProof = keyProofJWT($CI, pkH, ~skH)
  in
    [ Hon_St2($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skH, pkH, authSess, nonce), In(AT), Fr(~skE) ]
  --[ Hon_CredReq($Wid, $CI, ~sid, pkH) ]->
    [ Hon_St3($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skE, pkE, pkH),
      Out(<'cred-req', AT, pkH, keyProof, pkE>) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED
rule Hon_Client_CredReq [color=#bfdbfe, role="Wallet"]:
  let
    pkE      = pk(~skE)
    keyProof = keyProofJWT($CI, pkH, ~skH)
  in
    [ Hon_St2($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skH, pkH, authSess, nonce), In(AT), Fr(~skE) ]
  --[ Hon_CredReq($Wid, $CI, ~sid, pkH) ]->
    [ Hon_St3($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skE, pkE, pkH),
      Out(<'cred-req', AT, pkH, keyProof, pkE>) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED_NONCE
rule Hon_Client_CredReq [color=#bfdbfe, role="Wallet"]:
  let
    pkE      = pk(~skE)
    keyProof = keyProofJWTN($CI, pkH, nonce, ~skH)
  in
    [ Hon_St2($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skH, pkH, authSess, nonce), In(AT), Fr(~skE) ]
  --[ Hon_CredReq($Wid, $CI, ~sid, pkH) ]->
    [ Hon_St3($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skE, pkE, pkH),
      Out(<'cred-req', AT, pkH, keyProof, pkE>) ]
#endif

#ifdef FIXED_TXDATA
rule Hon_Client_CredReq [color=#bfdbfe, role="Wallet"]:
  let
    pkE      = pk(~skE)
    keyProof = keyProofJWT($CI, pkHiss, ~skHiss)
  in
    [ Hon_St2($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skH, pkH, authSess, nonce),
      !StoredIssuanceKey($Wid, ~skHiss, pkHiss),
      In(AT), Fr(~skE) ]
  --[ Hon_CredReq($Wid, $CI, ~sid, pkHiss) ]->
    [ Hon_St3($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skE, pkE, pkHiss),
      Out(<'cred-req', AT, pkHiss, keyProof, pkE>) ]
#endif

rule Hon_Client_RecvCred [color=#bfdbfe, role="Wallet"]:
  let
    encCred = penc(<'cred-resp', cred>, pk(~skE), rResp)
  in
    [ Hon_St3($Wid, $CI, ~sid, ~skE, pk(~skE), pkH_cred),
      In(encCred) ]
  --[ WalletObtained($Wid, $CI, pkH_cred, cred),
      Finish($Wid, $CI, ~sid) ]->
    [ ]


// ============================================================================
//   CREDENTIAL ENDPOINT   (one shape; configs differ only in the issuer check)
//   pkH_cred is the requester's submitted key, bound into the credential, and
//   recorded faithfully in CI_Issued in EVERY config.
// ============================================================================

// -------- VULNERABLE: no key check ------------------------------------------
#ifdef VULNERABLE
rule CI_Credential_Endpoint [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    cred    = credentialSig($CI, sub, pkH_cred, ~ltkCI)
    encCred = penc(<'cred-resp', cred>, pkE, ~rResp)
  in
    [ In(<'cred-req', AT, pkH_cred, keyProof, pkE>),
      !CI_Authorized($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      !Ltk_CI($CI, ~ltkCI),
      Fr(~rResp) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(keyProof, keyProofPayload($CI, pkH_cred), pkH_cred) = true ),
      OnlyOnceV(<'at-redeemed', AT>),
      CI_Issued($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) ]->
    [ Out(encCred) ]
#endif

// -------- FIXED_NONCE (NEGATIVE): key-proof binds the presentation nonce -----
#ifdef FIXED_NONCE
rule CI_Credential_Endpoint [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    cred    = credentialSig($CI, sub, pkH_cred, ~ltkCI)
    encCred = penc(<'cred-resp', cred>, pkE, ~rResp)
  in
    [ In(<'cred-req', AT, pkH_cred, keyProof, pkE>),
      !CI_Authorized($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      !Ltk_CI($CI, ~ltkCI),
      Fr(~rResp) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(keyProof, keyProofPayloadN($CI, pkH_cred, nonce), pkH_cred) = true ),
      OnlyOnceV(<'at-redeemed', AT>),
      CI_Issued($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) ]->
    [ Out(encCred) ]
#endif


#ifdef FIXED
rule CI_Credential_Endpoint [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    cred    = credentialSig($CI, sub, pkH_cred, ~ltkCI)
    encCred = penc(<'cred-resp', cred>, pkE, ~rResp)
  in
    [ In(<'cred-req', AT, pkH_cred, keyProof, pkE>),
      !CI_Authorized($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce),
      !Ltk_CI($CI, ~ltkCI),
      Fr(~rResp) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(keyProof, keyProofPayload($CI, pkH_cred), pkH_cred) = true ),
      Eq(pkH_cred, pkH_pres),
      OnlyOnceV(<'at-redeemed', AT>),
      CI_Issued($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) ]->
    [ Out(encCred) ]
#endif

// -------- FIXED_TXDATA: issued key must match the presenter's commitment -----
#ifdef FIXED_TXDATA
rule CI_Credential_Endpoint [color=#fef9c3, role="CI"]:
  let
    cred    = credentialSig($CI, sub, pkH_cred, ~ltkCI)
    encCred = penc(<'cred-resp', cred>, pkE, ~rResp)
  in
    [ In(<'cred-req', AT, pkH_cred, keyProof, pkE>),
      !CI_Authorized_Tx($CI, authSess, AT, pkH_pres, sub, nonce, cmt),
      !Ltk_CI($CI, ~ltkCI),
      Fr(~rResp) ]
  --[ _restrict( verify(keyProof, keyProofPayload($CI, pkH_cred), pkH_cred) = true ),
      Eq(cmt, h(pkH_cred)),
      OnlyOnceV(<'at-redeemed', AT>),
      CI_Issued($CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) ]->
    [ Out(encCred) ]
#endif


// ============================================================================
//                          HELPER LEMMAS  (all configs)
// ============================================================================

lemma ltkCI_secrecy [reuse, use_induction]:
  "All CI k #r #i.
       CIKey(CI, k) @ r & KU(k) @ i
     ==> (Ex #l. Reveal_CI(CI) @ l & l < i)"

lemma skH_secrecy [reuse, use_induction]:
  "All Wid skH pkH #r #i.
       VictimKeyFresh(Wid, skH, pkH) @ r & KU(skH) @ i
     ==> (Ex #l. Reveal_HolderKey(Wid, pkH) @ l & l < i)"

lemma holderkey_unique [reuse, use_induction]:
  "All Wid1 Wid2 skH1 skH2 pkH #i #j.
       VictimKeyFresh(Wid1, skH1, pkH) @ i
     & VictimKeyFresh(Wid2, skH2, pkH) @ j
     ==> #i = #j"


// ============================================================================
//                          EXECUTABILITY  (all configs)
// ============================================================================

lemma exec_honest_iae_flow:
  exists-trace
  "Ex Wid CI sid pkH_cred cred authSess pkH_pres sub #f #i.
        Finish(Wid, CI, sid) @ f
      & WalletObtained(Wid, CI, pkH_cred, cred) @ f
      & CI_Issued(CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) @ i
      & HonestCI(CI)"


// ============================================================================
//                              TACTICS
// ============================================================================

tactic: a1_witness_tactic
  presort: C
  prio:
    regex "CI_Issued\("
    regex "CI_Accepted_Presentation\("
    regex "Victim_Presented\("
    regex "AdversaryKey\("
    regex "!CI_Authorized"
    regex "!CI_IAE_Pending\("
  deprio:
    regex "!KU\( ~ltkCI"
    regex "!KU\( ~skH"
    regex "!KU\( ~"

tactic: a1_continuity_tactic
  presort: C
  prio:
    regex "CI_Issued\("
    regex "CI_Accepted_Presentation\("
    regex "Victim_Presented\("
    regex "Victim_Committed\("
    regex "Reveal_HolderKey\("
    regex "!CI_Authorized"
    regex "!CI_IAE_Pending\("
  deprio:
    regex "!KU\( ~ltkCI"
    regex "!KU\( ~skH"
    regex "!KU\( ~"

// serves a1_no_impersonation in both directions (counterexample + proof)
tactic: a1_impersonation_tactic
  presort: C
  prio:
    regex "CI_Issued\("
    regex "AdversaryKey\("
    regex "CI_Accepted_Presentation\("
    regex "Victim_Presented\("
    regex "Victim_Committed\("
    regex "!CI_Authorized"
    regex "!CI_IAE_Pending\("
  deprio:
    regex "!KU\( ~ltkCI"
    regex "!KU\( ~skH"
    regex "!KU\( ~"


lemma a1_no_impersonation [heuristic={a1_impersonation_tactic}]:
  "not (Ex CI authSess Wid pkH_pres sub pkH_cred cred skH #iss #v #adv.
            CI_Issued(CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) @ iss
          & VictimKeyFresh(Wid, skH, pkH_pres) @ v
          & AdversaryKey(pkH_cred) @ adv
          & (not (Ex #r. Reveal_CI(CI) @ r))
          & (not (Ex #r. Reveal_HolderKey(Wid, pkH_pres) @ r)) )"


// ============================================================================
//   VULNERABLE  —  the attack + the falsified holder-continuity property
// ============================================================================

#ifdef VULNERABLE


lemma a1_attack_witness [heuristic={a1_witness_tactic}]:
  exists-trace
  "Ex CI authSess Wid pkH_pres sub nonce pkH_cred cred skH
      #v #pres #iss #adv #k.
        VictimKeyFresh(Wid, skH, pkH_pres) @ v
      & Victim_Presented(Wid, CI, pkH_pres, sub, nonce) @ pres
      & CI_Issued(CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) @ iss
      & AdversaryKey(pkH_cred) @ adv
      & K(cred) @ k
      & not (pkH_cred = pkH_pres)
      & (not (Ex c #r. Reveal_CI(c) @ r))
      & (not (Ex W p #r. Reveal_HolderKey(W, p) @ r))"

lemma a1_holder_continuity_vuln [heuristic={a1_continuity_tactic}]:
  "All CI authSess Wid pkH_pres sub pkH_cred cred skH #iss #v.
        CI_Issued(CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) @ iss
      & VictimKeyFresh(Wid, skH, pkH_pres) @ v
      & HonestCI(CI)
      & NoHolderKeyLeak(Wid, pkH_pres)
      ==> pkH_cred = pkH_pres"

#endif


// ============================================================================
//   FIXED_NONCE  (NEGATIVE RESULT)  —  nonce binding does not close A1
// ============================================================================

#ifdef FIXED_NONCE

lemma a1_holder_continuity_nonce [heuristic={a1_continuity_tactic}]:
  "All CI authSess Wid pkH_pres sub pkH_cred cred skH #iss #v.
        CI_Issued(CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) @ iss
      & VictimKeyFresh(Wid, skH, pkH_pres) @ v
      & HonestCI(CI)
      & NoHolderKeyLeak(Wid, pkH_pres)
      ==> pkH_cred = pkH_pres"

#endif


// ============================================================================
//   FIXED  —  holder-key continuity closes A1
// ============================================================================

#ifdef FIXED

lemma a1_holder_continuity_fixed [heuristic={a1_continuity_tactic}]:
  "All CI authSess Wid pkH_pres sub pkH_cred cred skH #iss #v.
        CI_Issued(CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) @ iss
      & VictimKeyFresh(Wid, skH, pkH_pres) @ v
      & HonestCI(CI)
      & NoHolderKeyLeak(Wid, pkH_pres)
      ==> pkH_cred = pkH_pres"

#endif


// ============================================================================
//   FIXED_TXDATA  —  authorised issuance key closes A1 (allows key separation)
// ============================================================================

#ifdef FIXED_TXDATA

lemma a1_holder_authorization_txdata [heuristic={a1_continuity_tactic}]:
  "All CI authSess Wid pkH_pres sub pkH_cred cred skH #iss #v.
        CI_Issued(CI, authSess, pkH_pres, sub, pkH_cred, cred) @ iss
      & VictimKeyFresh(Wid, skH, pkH_pres) @ v
      & HonestCI(CI)
      & NoHolderKeyLeak(Wid, pkH_pres)
      ==> (Ex #c. Victim_Committed(Wid, pkH_cred) @ c)"

#endif


end

